From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:41:21 -0400
Subject: [M152] [SkPath] Increase GenerationID to 64 bits

Original change's description:
> [SkPath] Increase GenerationID to 64 bits
>
> * GenerationID was originally intended to be a modification tracker per object but became conflated with global uniqueness. This was fine so long as ID usages were sufficiently temporally separated that wrapping IDs would never collide. However, at 32 bits it is feasible for an attacker to cause wrapping in a relatively small amount of time.
>
> * This patch ups the GenerationID to 64 bits
>
> Bug: b/562038679
> Bug: b/556268833
> Change-Id: I12d2e93cc32c8922fe0b19a1f737e6196ed54dd8
> Reviewed-on: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1366216
> Reviewed-by: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
> Commit-Queue: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>

(cherry picked from commit 76f502419c33e910b98248e749ed55185ab81a99)

Bug: 567398505,b/562038679,b/556268833
Change-Id: I12d2e93cc32c8922fe0b19a1f737e6196ed54dd8

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): the Gerrit auto-cherry-pick of this
change onto chrome/m152 (patch set 2) left an unresolved Git conflict in
the system-include block of src/core/SkPathData.cpp, because chrome/m152
does not contain the "#include <array>" line the upstream hunk was
anchored to. Resolved by keeping the m152 include block and adding only
"#include <limits>", which is the sole line the upstream change inserts
there. No other hunk was modified.

